[Term]
id: ECAO:2000104
name: vegetal pole
namespace: echinoderm_anatomy
def: "The most apical region of the vegetal hemisphere. Among echinoderms, in euechinoids, once cleavages have started, the vegetal pole is characterized by the presence of the micromeres initially and then that of the small micromeres. Subsequently, it is marked by the site of ingression of the primary mesenchyme cells (PMCs), and finally in all echinoderms by the site of invagination and presence of the blastopore." []
