[Term]
id: ECAO:2000117
name: cilium
namespace: echinoderm_anatomy
def: "A specialized organelle that consists of a filiform extrusion of the cell surface and of some cytoplasmic parts. Each cilium is largely bounded by an extrusion of the cytoplasmic (plasma) membrane, and contains a regular longitudinal array of microtubules, anchored to a basal body." []
synonym: "flagellum" RELATED []
